510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E ( It allows a method to act differently depending on the specific object that calls it. The parent class FileReaderWriter has a default read\(\) method that just prints a message and returns an empty list. The child class CSVFileReaderWriter overrides this method by using the exact same name but replacing the inside logic with instructions to analyze spreadsheet files. When the code calls read\(\), python runs the specific child version instead of the default parent layout. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
