565 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 295 0 R
/E (The group built a PyQt6 desktop application called the Laboratory Equipment Borrowing and Inventory Management System. It replaces the paper borrowing slip with a digital process. A student submits a request, the professor approves or declines it, the laboratory staff release and receive the items, and ITSO keeps a record of every slip in a CSV file. The program also keeps the inventory updated when items are added, released and returned. It has a login for each role, a menu bar, dialogs, a QSS theme, and it was packaged as a Windows .exe. All 30 test cases passed, and four of the five objectives were fully met. Objective 2 was partly met because the student ID and name are only checked if they are empty.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
566 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 295 0 R
/E (The application answers the problem in the paper. Students no longer need to fill out a slip by hand or line up just to find out an item is not available, because they can search the stock and track the request. Professors can approve from the dashboard, and the staff can see the approved requests. ITSO has an organized record with the submitted and returned times, so it is easier to know who borrowed what. The OOP principles were also applied through the file reader classes, the data classes, the inventory manager, and the separate UI and logic classes. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
